     from Apache FOP 2.11: a test of hook page-number-restart (fop/CR-017.2). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      Other shapes of fox:page-number-restart. First sequence: the restarting part opens page 3, which prints the
      restart number, 5. Second: a part with no restart after a restarting one continues its count, and a citation
      of a block on a renumbered page gives the number that page prints. Third: a restart at 0, where the user
      agent does not allow a page numbered 0, numbers the part's count from 1, as initial-page-number does.
      Fourth: a following page-sequence with initial-page-number="auto" continues from the number the third's
      last page prints.
    </p>
  </info>
